r"""patch_L443_20_comets_20261026.py -- the comets on open paths come to the orrery's export (L-443,
slice 2, build B part 2), with the comet nucleus sizes sourced (L-491).

Built on orrery 5398439591f35979c4df1791e25477ac37119b01 at
https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/palomas_orrery (branch main), AFTER
patch_L485_1_records_and_compositions_20261026.py has run. Its website
half is the gallery's patch_L443_21_comets_room_20261026.py, run after
this one is pushed.

WHAT IT EDITS, all or nothing

    celestial_objects.py: the fourteen comets keyed, each marked
        open_path, with JPL's name and its approved description; West
        asked as C/1975 V1-A.
    path_plan.py and test_path_plan.py: each comet on an open path is
        planned from a year before its perihelion to a year after today,
        inside JPL's data, its perihelion found in JPL's positions; the
        spacecraft plans do not search comets.
    export_objects.py, period_fetch.py: a comet on an open path is a
        path, and serves no period.
    horizons_check.py and test_horizons_check.py: an entry asked by
        JPL's number is looked for in the small-body lookup; a path
        confirms no period.
    constants_new.py, comet_visualization_shells.py,
        data/provenance_exceptions.json: L-491, the nine sourced nucleus
        sizes; the six with no open source print none.
        provenance_scanner.py: its note of known exceptions no longer
        names the table, which is gone; no code changed.
    skills/: interactive-exhibit 1.26, horizons-orbital-mechanics 1.12,
        gallery-cache-builder 1.13. PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS.md v3.114 and
        its manifest; the two history files.
    LEDGER_CONSOLIDATED.md: L-443's progress and Gap; L-491 and L-492
        new; L-490's first question; the header stamp.
    documentation/WHERE_WE_ARE.md: the header, the box, the road, the
        Settled, Deferred and Waiting lines, the details.
    New: documentation/CHECK_L491_comet_nucleus_sizes_20261026.md and
        documentation/HANDOFF_L443_slice2_buildB_comets_20261026.md.

HOW TO RUN

    Save it in the orrery folder (palomas_orrery_for_github), open it in
    VS Code and press Run (the same as python patch_L443_20_comets_20261026.py from that folder). It
    asks nothing, prints an "ok" line per file, then "patch applied". A
    second run refuses. Then orrery_maintenance_run.py: its path plan row
    plans the fourteen comets from JPL (a few minutes, a line as each
    answer comes), and the Horizons check confirms their names. Move
    this file into documentation\, commit and push. Undo before a commit
    is Discard Changes in GitHub Desktop.

Written October 26, 2026 with Anthropic's Claude Opus 5.5.
"""
